<title>CANADA: Canada government cash balances fall in week.</title>
<headline>Canada government cash balances fall in week.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The government of Canada's cash balances fell in the week that ended August 28, the Bank of Canada said on Friday.</p>
<p>				    Wk to Aug 28  Chg on wk Chg on yr</p>
<p>Notes in circulation		  27.35   +0.435    +0.237</p>
<p>Government cash balances	     3.54   -0.629    +0.089</p>
<p>Govt securities outstanding	463.73   +1.660   +10.436</p>
<p>Treasury bills			 152.80   +0.300   -11.900</p>
<p>Canada savings bonds		  30.12   -0.004    +0.578</p>
<p>All figures in billions of dollars.  </p>
<p>Chartered bank assets			   July	  June</p>
<p>   Net foreign currency			-12.63	-12.08</p>
<p>   Canadian dollar			     639.55	639.38</p>
<p>   Total Canadian liquid assets	    107.83	107.24</p>
<p>					 July 96    June 96     July 95</p>
<p>M1					 63.02	62.83	57.50</p>
<p>M2					389.79     391.32     381.65</p>
<p>M3					482.13     480.72     461.42</p>
<p>Note - Figures are unadjusted, in billions of dollars.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Ottawa Bureau (613) 235-6745</p>
</text>
